---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { base } from '../../utils/base';
const ids=["finops/budgets-cost-caps-and-the-lie-of-spending-limits","finops/discounts-and-commitments-math-the-salespeople-hope-you-wont-do","finops/cloud-support-what-you-are-actually-paying-for"];
const articles=await getCollection('knowledgeBase');
const reading=ids.map(id=>{const a=articles.find(a=>a.id===id);if(!a)throw new Error('Missing cost reading: '+id);return a;});
const sources=[["Build a workload cost model","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/well-architected/cost-optimization/cost-model"],["VM states and remaining charges","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/states-billing"],["Autoscaling bounds and behaviour","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/autoscale/autoscale-best-practices"],["Azure transfer pricing by route","https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/details/bandwidth/"],["Oracle service price list","https://www.oracle.com/cloud/price-list/"],["Budgets notify; consumption continues","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/costs/tutorial-acm-create-budgets"]];
---
<section class="cost-reading" aria-labelledby="cost-reading-title">
  <h2 id="cost-reading-title">Read the detail behind the decision.</h2>
  <p>These three existing articles have been fact-checked and revised: what budgets enforce, when commitments save, and what support leaves your team to do.</p>
  <ul role="list">{reading.map(a=><li><a href={base+'/knowledge-base/'+a.id}>{a.data.title} &rarr;</a><p>{a.data.excerpt}</p></li>)}</ul>
  <aside>
    <h3>Sources &amp; method</h3>
    <p>Reviewed 11 September 2026. The illustrations are qualitative examples, not a billing simulation. The checklist uses your answers to identify measurements and planning gaps. It does not query your cloud account, use live prices or calculate savings. Price the selected services using current regional rates and your contract.</p>
    <ul role="list">{sources.map(([label,href])=><li><a href={href}>{label} &rarr;</a></li>)}</ul>
  </aside>
</section>
<style>
  h2 { font: var(--weight-semibold) var(--text-headline-md)/var(--leading-snug) var(--font-display); letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight); }
  p { margin-top: var(--space-3); max-width: 80ch; color: var(--color-on-surface-muted); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); }
  ul { display: grid; gap: var(--space-5); margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  a { color: var(--color-navy); font-weight: var(--weight-semibold); }
  aside { margin-top: var(--space-7); padding: var(--space-5); background: var(--color-surface-container-low); }
  h3 { color: var(--color-primary); font: var(--text-label-md) var(--font-mono); }
  aside a, aside p { font-size: var(--text-label-md); }
  @media(min-width:768px){aside ul{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}}
</style>
